  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-17T01:30:48.311Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I was recently pondering ways to mitigate toxicity and avoid bad actors in VRChat and was inspired by Bluesky's \"mute list\" feature.\n\nFor those who aren't aware, the feature allows for anyone to add people to a list, where others can then subscribe to it and automatically mute everyone inside. It's really great for muting NFT accounts, known bigots, etc. (I attached a screenshot of what this looks like.)\n\nI think this solution could translate pretty elegantly to VRChat. Perhaps it could integrate into Groups, allowing group members to opt-in to muting users the group admins have banned? Or maybe a separate list entirely? Something like that.\n\nUsing the Trans group as an example: When highlighting a transphobic user, (even outside of a group instance!) a moderator of the Trans group could hit \"Add to mute list\" and select their group. Anyone in the Trans group who is then opted-in to syncing with the group's mute list will also have that person muted upon running into them in the wild.\n\nLet me know what you think!\n\nNote: I wanted to add that I'm very aware this could lead to abuse from group moderators and cause all sorts of trouble. While I do agree that will inevitably happen in some circumstances, I don't think it completely devalues the idea because ultimately it's up to you to only subscribe to lists from trustworthy sources and people/organizations whose values and judgment you trust. I'm not 100% onboard with this idea myself either, I just thought it was an interesting method of dealing with toxicity.)",
